**9 Best Concerts and Festivals of Spring**

__Open-Air in Kraljevo, Skillet on the banks of the Danube and Lenny Kravitz (legendary, what else is there to say)__

__Part II__

**Skillet**

Skillet is one of the most notable bands at the intersection of nu-metal and alternative hard rock, which managed to break into the mainstream: over 20 years of career, the band released platinum albums and received two Grammy Award nominations. In May, Belgrade awaits a powerful show with a signature stadium production and heavy symphonic sound, for which the group has been loved by the whole world.

Hangar (Luka Beograd) • Žorža Klemansoa 37 • May 16 • 7:00 PM • from 5900 RSD • ${PLACEHOLDER_1} 

**Changeover Tour**

Changeover Festival has become one of the most anticipated music events in the region in recent years. And this year it starts with a spring pop-up tour of Europe: Belgrade starts on May 22-23, then there will be Nis, Sofia, Zagreb, Prague and Berlin. The lineup and list of locations will be announced soon, but we are already sure that it will be cool, so it's time to buy tickets!

Various locations, Belgrade • May 22-23 • from 1600 RSD • ${PLACEHOLDER_2} 

**Anthrax**

Anthrax, a member of the "big four" of thrash metal alongside Metallica, Slayer and Megadeth, is returning with a program of the best hits from 40 years of career. The setlist includes Madhouse, Indians and other classic tracks that made them one of the key figures in the genre.

OpenAir Corner (Luka Beograd) • Žorža Klemansoa 37 • May 29 • 7:00 PM • from 5700 RSD • ${PLACEHOLDER_3} 

**Belgrade River Fest**

A two-day open-air event on the banks of the Sava River with a multi-genre program and an emphasis on scale shows. This year's headliner is Ricky Martin, the author of __Livin’ La Vida Loca__ and one of the leading pop artists of the 2000s. The lineup also includes pop, Latin and electronic music, and light shows and fireworks will complete the atmosphere.

Kula Plaza • June 16-17 • 9:00 PM • from 4500 RSD • ${PLACEHOLDER_4} 

**Lenny Kravitz**

Lenny Kravitz, one of the leading rock icons of recent decades, will perform in Belgrade with a big live show. His signature mix of rock, funk and soul, multiplied by stage charisma, turns concerts into a non-stop hit parade: from Are You Gonna Go My Way to Fly Away.

Park Ušće • June 17 • 8:00 PM • from 7500 RSD • ${PLACEHOLDER_5} 

 ${PLACEHOLDER_6}

9 Best Spring Concerts and Festivals
__Open-air in Kraljevo, Skillet by the Danube and Lenny Kravitz (legendary, what else can you say) __

__Part I__

**Kontakt Festival**

The three-day city festival Kontakt, which unites key Belgrade club and cultural venues, will be held for the 10th time. The program features techno, house, and experimental electronics from local and international artists. Electropionir will host a vinyl fair with live sets, Drugstore will host nightly raves, and Dorćol Platz will feature Croatian hip-hop band The Beat Fleet (on Friday) and iconic rockers LET 3, who have been provocative since the Yugoslav era (on Saturday).

Electropionir, Dorćol Platz, Drugstore and other venues • April 16–18 • from 2000 RSD • ${PLACEHOLDER_1}

**Fields Music Festival**

A festival of inventive music and media art, which always surprises and encourages you to step out of your comfort zone and discover new names—and sometimes even entire art movements. More than ten artists have already been announced, including British electronic music pioneer Xylitol, krautrockers Skier & Yeti, French sound designer Hélène Vogelsinger, and the most unusual event of the festival: the performance "Borders", created by a Serbian-Russian team of musicians, choreographers, and artists.

Karmakoma, Bioskop Balkan, EJE Belgrade • April 16–18 • 7:00 PM • from 31 EUR • ${PLACEHOLDER_2}

**Hugh Cornwell**

Hugh Cornwall, the iconic British guitarist and frontman of the punk-new wave band The Stranglers, will perform at Zappa Baza — concerts of this scale are rare! It was Hugh who was behind the band's biggest hits—from Peaches and No More Heroes to the iconic Golden Brown, cementing his reputation as one of the most original authors of the British scene. After leaving The Stranglers, Cornwell successfully continued his solo career: his later albums Monster (2016) and Moments of Madness (2022) received rave reviews from critics.

Zappa Baza • Bulevar Vojvode Bojovića 30a • April 26 • 8:00 PM • from 3200 RSD • ${PLACEHOLDER_3} 

**Under Grad Festival**

Opening the season of open-air festivals: three days at the foot of the medieval Maglič fortress - what else could you dream of for May Day?  The festival will be opened by Bam Bam kolektiv, also in the lineup this year will be folk band Ko to tamo vera, Nataleé, Turbo Trans turisti, who recently released a new album, techno from White sity soul… In general, the whole color of the local scene will gather, and there will also be a campsite, a market of local brands and an evening bonfire.

Tvrđava Maglič, Kraljevo • April 30—May 2 • from 3290 RSD • ${PLACEHOLDER_4} 

